# Agent attention

Agent harnesses should render right-aligned lifecycle summaries on their
session rows and in aggregate on the header. Waiting, failed, and succeeded
harnesses should use the same attention pip styling as a tmux bell; running and
idle harnesses should not. A manual flag on a session that also has agent
attention should retain the existing attention-over-flag precedence.

Create one session per lifecycle state, with extra panes and windows in the
waiting, succeeded, and running sessions to exercise aggregation. Flag the
succeeded session so attention and manual-flag styling compete on the same row.

    :b jj cat (available)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s waiting "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t waiting:0.0 @smth.agent.state waiting (success)
    :t split-window -d -t waiting:0 "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t waiting:0.1 @smth.agent.state running (success)
    :t new-window -d -t waiting: -n worker "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t waiting:1.0 @smth.agent.state running (success)
    :t new-session -d -s failed "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t failed:0.0 @smth.agent.state failed (success)
    :t new-session -d -s succeeded "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t succeeded:0.0 @smth.agent.state succeeded (success)
    :t split-window -d -t succeeded:0 "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t succeeded:0.1 @smth.agent.state succeeded (success)
    :t new-window -d -t succeeded: -n ready "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t succeeded:1.0 @smth.agent.state idle (success)
    :t set-option -t succeeded @smth.flag 1 (success)
    :t new-session -d -s running "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t running:0.0 @smth.agent.state running (success)
    :t split-window -d -t running:0 "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t running:0.1 @smth.agent.state running (success)
    :t new-session -d -s idle "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t idle:0.0 @smth.agent.state idle (success)

    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 100 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Hide the preview so every session is visible in one snapshot. The linked colour
snapshots distinguish lifecycle states and attention, flag, and ordinary
live-session pips. Status indicators and counts should remain undimmed.

    :k C-p
    :snap --color

```terminal
session:                                                                                           ┃
  7/7 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                  ⏸ · × · ✔ 2 · ▶ 4 · ○ 2 ┃
▌■ runner                                                                                          ┃
 ■ failed                                                                                        × ┃
 ■ idle                                                                                          ○ ┃
 ■ running                                                                                     ▶ 2 ┃
 ■ succeeded                                                                               ✔ 2 · ○ ┃
 ■ waiting                                                                                 ⏸ · ▶ 2 ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                                                           ┃
```

![light](agent-attention.md.snap.1.light.svg)
![dark](agent-attention.md.snap.1.dark.svg)

Filter to a session with successful agent responses. The header summary should
continue to aggregate agents across every session while the selected row shows
only that session's agents. In the linked colour snapshots, the success glyph
should remain bright green without creating a green background cell.

    :k succeeded
    :snap --color

```terminal
session: succeeded                                                                                 ┃
  1/7 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                  ⏸ · × · ✔ 2 · ▶ 4 · ○ 2 ┃
   succeeded~1                              ~/succeeded                                       repo ┃
   succeeded~1                                                                                tmux ┃
▌■ succeeded                                                                               ✔ 2 · ○ ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] unflag                                                                         ┃
```

![light](agent-attention.md.snap.2.light.svg)
![dark](agent-attention.md.snap.2.dark.svg)

Add a running agent outside the current query, then close the selected succeeded
session to trigger rediscovery. The global summary should include the new agent
and remove both succeeded agents and their idle sibling, without doubling the
counts of surviving sessions.

    :t new-session -d -s extra "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t extra:0.0 @smth.agent.state running (success)
    :t set-hook -g session-closed "set-hook -gu session-closed; wait-for -S closed-succeeded" (success)
    :k C-x
    :t wait-for closed-succeeded (success)
    :snap -e '0/7'

```terminal
session: succeeded                                                                                 ┃
  0/7 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                          ⏸ · × · ▶ 5 · ○ ┃
   succeeded                                ~/succeeded                                       repo ┃
▌  succeeded                                                                                  tmux ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
```

Close the newly discovered session as well. A second rediscovery should remove
its running agent while retaining the original sessions' counts.

    :k C-u extra
    :settle -e '1/7' (settled)
    :t set-hook -g session-closed "set-hook -gu session-closed; wait-for -S closed-extra" (success)
    :k C-x
    :t wait-for closed-extra (success)
    :snap -e '0/6'

```terminal
session: extra                                                                                     ┃
  0/6 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                          ⏸ · × · ▶ 4 · ○ ┃
   extra                                    ~/extra                                           repo ┃
▌  extra                                                                                      tmux ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
```

